  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts`, which implements the click-to-plant garden. It typechecks, but I couldn't build or run it in a browser here, so the rendering, shadows, click picking and frame rate are untested.\n\n**Scene.** It uses the `outdoor-day` look (sky, sun shadow, fog) with a 16×16 grass plane on a soil border. The camera looks down at an angle so the whole plot is in view. I set `pixelRatio: 1` after spreading `looks.appOptions`, which otherwise asks for 2x, so the canvas isn't resized.\n\n**Click to plant.** A click is converted to a ray from the camera and intersected with the y=0 ground plane. The ray math is my own, using the same camera position, target, vertical FOV and canvas aspect I passed to the engine. Clicks on the sky or outside ±8 are ignored.\n\n**Plants.**\n- **Drawing:** all plants are drawn as four instanced primitives (stems, leaves, petals, flower centres), so 200 plants cost four draw calls plus the ground. Instance matrices and colours are rewritten each frame only while a plant is still growing, or after a plant or clear.\n- **Growth:** each plant grows from a pale sprout with two small leaves into a taller, darker plant with four leaves and a flower over 8 seconds. Later plants are smaller than earlier ones. Flower colour, centre colour, flower size and height vary per plant.\n- **Cap:** at most 200 plants, and the oldest is dropped past that.\n\n**Overlay and page API.**\n- **Overlay:** a top-left DOM overlay shows `Plants: N` and a `Clear` button.\n- **`window.__TASK_STATE__`:** a frozen, read-only object whose getters return `plantCount`, `plants` as `{x, z, growth}` (live growth from 0 to 1) and `ready`.\n- **`window.__plantAt(x, z)`:** plants at those ground coordinates and returns false if they are not finite or lie outside ±8.\n- **Ready flags:** `ready` and `window.__EVAL_READY__` are set a frame after the first frames render.\n\n**Zero plants.** The instanced nodes always include four tiny hidden corner instances, so they are never empty at zero pla",
